{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"694a737b4b78ed15","type":"text","text":"# Vehicle\n","x":-240,"y":-1120,"width":410,"height":396},
		{"id":"f3f4990fa06decce","type":"text","text":"# **Files**\n","x":567,"y":-136,"width":440,"height":396},
		{"id":"8dc3ae16a8d044ef","type":"text","text":"\n# Listing\n","x":-1040,"y":-136,"width":450,"height":396},
		{"id":"2f77c1d315d01ffd","type":"text","text":"## Process\n- User selects a file (image or PDF) on the Next.js frontend (Mantine FileInput).\n- The frontend calls your NestJS backend asking for a pre-signed upload URL.\n- NestJS generates the pre-signed URL from DigitalOcean Spaces and returns:\n\t- uploadUrl → temporary URL where the file can be uploaded.\n\t- fileUrl → permanent public (or private) file URL in Spaces.\n- The frontend uses axios.put() to upload the file directly to Spaces, bypassing the backend.\n- Once upload succeeds, the frontend calls your NestJS /files endpoint to save file metadata (vehicle_id, file_url, mime_type, size, type=image/pdf) into PostgreSQL.\n- The vehicle listing page fetches file metadata from PostgreSQL and displays images/PDF links using the fileUrl.","x":-31,"y":568,"width":631,"height":392},
		{"id":"340258be667fafca","type":"text","text":"## Entitiy fields/metadata\n- file_id (PK)\n- vehicle_id (FK → Vehicle.vehicle_id)\n- file_type (image | pdf)\n- file_name\n- file_url \n- mime_type (image/jpeg, application/pdf, etc.)\n- size_bytes\n- uploaded_at\n- is_primary (boolean, e.g. main display photo)","x":1160,"y":568,"width":440,"height":344}
	],
